the target language is: lps.

% Wolf, goat, cabbage and farmer. Composite events with recursive decomposition.
% Source: legacy_lps1/examples/goat.pl

the maximum time is 8.

the events are:
    *an object* is moved to *a place*; known as makeLoc.
    the goat is dealt with from *a first place* to *a second place*; known as dealWithGoat.

the actions are:
    the farmer rows from *a first place* to *a second place*; known as row.
    *an object* is carried from *a first place* to *a second place*; known as transport.

the fluents are:
    *an object* is at *a place*; known as loc.

the knowledge base goat includes:

initially the wolf is at south
    and the goat is at south
    and the cabbage is at south
    and the farmer is at south.

if an object is at south at a first time
    and the object is different from the farmer
then the object is moved to north from a second time to a third time.

an object is moved to a first place from a first time to a third time if
    the object is different from the farmer
    and the object is at a second place at the first time
    and the first place is different from the second place
    and the farmer is moved to the second place from the first time to a second time
    and the farmer rows from the second place to the first place from the second time to the third time
    and the object is carried from the second place to the first place from the second time to the third time
    and the goat is dealt with from the second place to the first place from the second time to the third time.

the farmer is moved to a first place from a first time to a third time if
    the farmer is at a second place at the first time
    and the first place is different from the second place
    and the farmer rows from the second place to the first place to the first time
    and the goat is dealt with from the second place to the first place from the first time to the third time.

the goat is dealt with from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time if
    it is not the case that the goat is at the first place at the first time.

the goat is dealt with from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time if
    it is not the case that the wolf is at the first place at the first time
    and it is not the case that the cabbage is at the first place at the first time.

the goat is dealt with from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time if
    the goat is at the first place at the first time
    and the wolf is at the first place at the first time
    and the goat is carried from the first place to the second place from the first time to the second time.

the goat is dealt with from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time if
    the goat is at the first place at the first time
    and the wolf is at the first place at the first time
    and it is not the case that the cabbage is at the first place at the first time
    and the wolf is carried from the first place to the second place from the first time to the second time.

the goat is dealt with from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time if
    the goat is at the first place at the first time
    and the cabbage is at the first place at the first time
    and the goat is carried from the first place to the second place from the first time to the second time.

the goat is dealt with from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time if
    the goat is at the first place at the first time
    and the cabbage is at the first place at the first time
    and it is not the case that the wolf is at the first place at the first time
    and the cabbage is carried from the first place to the second place from the first time to the second time.

an object is moved to a place from a first time to the first time if
    the object is at the place at the first time.

when an object is carried from a first place to a second place
then the object is at the second place.

when an object is carried from a first place to a second place
then it is not the case that the object is at the first place.

when the farmer rows from a first place to a second place
then the farmer is at the second place.

when the farmer rows from a first place to a second place
then it is not the case that the farmer is at the first place.

it must not be true that
    a first object is carried from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time
    and a second object is carried from the first place to the second place from the first time to the second time
    and the first object is different from the second object.

it must not be true that
    the farmer rows from south to north from a first time to a second time
    and the farmer rows from north to south from the first time to the second time.
